    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0633" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/25: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China
                        (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-08T12:00:00-05:00">March 8, 1932—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Your 312, March 8, 11 a.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Department has telegraphed the Consul General at Harbin<anchor n="64"
                            xml:id="d569-f1"/> directly that he should not attend congratulatory
                        celebration and should file without acknowledgment any official invitation
                        received from the new regime.</item>
                    <pb facs="0634" n="530" xml:id="pg530"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Please inform Consul General at Mukden that Department approves his
                        attitude toward invitation to attend inauguration of the executive at
                        Changchun and that he should file invitation without acknowledgment.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Inform Minister.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
